<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:43:31Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Saudi Arabia: Rights groups raise alarm over rising number of executions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8705774d27433d8a3732780cd4a48925968c502bde8ac1f7bf360ad6f004a1ef</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:42:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T17:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-rights-groups-raise-alarm-over-rising-number-of-executions/a-79970773--88ad6ac6f724.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-rights-groups-raise-alarm-over-rising-number-of-executions/a-79970773?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amid the war in Iran, Saudi Arabia's human rights situation remains bleak, with at least 211 executions, corporal punishment and an intensifying crackdown on critics. Is the regional conflict driving domestic repression?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US and Mexico lose measles-free status</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19fe90162afd6df46dcbbfd2080800b3168572968f6882c0993a00689e7c456d</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:42:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T16:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-and-mexico-lose-measles-free-status/a-79973966--f59bc5b58da7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-and-mexico-lose-measles-free-status/a-79973966?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The United States lost its measles elimination status after 26 years, the Pan American Health Organization has said. Bolivia and Mexico have also lost their measles elimination status.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's growing exodus of young talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:419a77fff068ff7dd0d9566606068efb854b1613b813a2bb2ffd12d0ff3c6605</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:41:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368--aa300b774c88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflict and uncertainty are driving more and more educated young Iranians to consider leaving the country.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Back to 1997: Russia wants NATO to roll back its eastern expansion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23b315343456b4e28d7707b1682a13e37c312cd7a57783976a16c87a19c289e2</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T16:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/back-to-1997-russia-wants-nato-to-roll-back-its-eastern-expansion/a-79970289--e5e38f4e75de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/back-to-1997-russia-wants-nato-to-roll-back-its-eastern-expansion/a-79970289?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Kremlin is reportedly calling on NATO to withdraw from large parts of Eastern Europe. What this would mean for the security of millions of Europeans — and what lies behind Russia's plan.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Rights court rules Turkey must release jailed lawmaker Atalay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee8cef3309856593fb72742e38678ce6a64b2cd6646b0acb1b7ce8872dc3e99b</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T15:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rights-court-rules-turkey-must-release-jailed-lawmaker-atalay/a-79972462--8247972e6110.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rights-court-rules-turkey-must-release-jailed-lawmaker-atalay/a-79972462?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Court of Human Rights has called for the release of imprisoned elected lawmaker Can Atalay. Atalay has been in prison for almost five years despite rulings from the Turkish Constitutional Court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fresh clashes at the Eritrean border — is Ethiopia sliding into a regional war?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb7b8a92ebef02fdeb73e1e0d2fe24c69498151df73d99eb4111f94e47f10eb5</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:42:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T15:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fresh-clashes-at-the-eritrean-border-is-ethiopia-sliding-into-a-regional-war/a-79970353--d3d8ce7621b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fresh-clashes-at-the-eritrean-border-is-ethiopia-sliding-into-a-regional-war/a-79970353?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Ethiopian troops push Tigrayan forces toward the Eritrean border, fears of a new regional war are growing. With tensions rising between Ethiopia, Eritrea and Sudan, the Horn of Africa faces uncertain times ahead.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia forms national security committee after Huang affair</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:713ef08afc83e04d0e7c44b036f422c2f3c03a8612b0e6fa65c7fe3942f3ba43</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:42:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T14:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-forms-national-security-committee-after-huang-affair/a-79970447--7d1c93df3ff0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-forms-national-security-committee-after-huang-affair/a-79970447?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia has created a board-level committee for national security and export control. This follows the resignation of CEO Jensen Huang over extramarital affairs, allegedly including one with a Chinese intelligence asset.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran dismisses report of alleged 'dirty bomb' attack on Washington</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59cadc11def66217b426968d17d95c405abf0f146eadf4860beea999fbf50427</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T14:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-dismisses-report-of-alleged-dirty-bomb-attack-on-washington/a-79970741--39825cf9b7d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-dismisses-report-of-alleged-dirty-bomb-attack-on-washington/a-79970741?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran has said CNN's claim that Tehran would attack Washington with a "dirty bomb" was an attempt to manufacture further legitimacy to continue the war. Trump has said his administration takes the claim "very seriously."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>APEC summit: What Trump, Xi and Putin want</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e607961938060d798f128067846bbb694492590591c4300ed7e0975fc8eafadc</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:43:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/apec-summit-what-trump-xi-and-putin-want/a-79970462--5ebb76396afb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/apec-summit-what-trump-xi-and-putin-want/a-79970462?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trump, Xi and Putin will hold their first trilateral meeting on the sidelines of APEC. With different priorities on trade, Ukraine, Iran and arms control, what does each leader hope to gain?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU, ASEAN pursue deeper trade ties, but hurdles remain as businesses struggle with informal barriers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b81ee2d096cc71ebe29017b534214e495f174027f0e5a351ee235a927d8068a</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:43:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T14:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-asean-pursue-deeper-trade-ties-but-hurdles-remain-as-businesses-struggle-with-informal-barriers/a-79971350--2638efb19213.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-asean-pursue-deeper-trade-ties-but-hurdles-remain-as-businesses-struggle-with-informal-barriers/a-79971350?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">2027 could be a landmark year for EU–Southeast Asia trade, with several deals nearing completion. But the harder task will be to ensure that businesses actually use them.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Guinea jails 200 in wildcat gold mining crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eaa61f8ef47226a058053a1d6cfef7fd2c2c34eebb5d191cc9047ce7d9e1c161</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:43:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T12:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/guinea-jails-200-in-wildcat-gold-mining-crackdown/a-79968808--52f221020a34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/guinea-jails-200-in-wildcat-gold-mining-crackdown/a-79968808?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Conakry court has jailed 22 former local officials from the gold-rich northeastern Siguiri region, as well as 200 people accused of illegal mining. It's part of a wider crackdown that sent thousands fleeing into Mali.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US flexes climate action muscle at COP31 despite Trump no-show</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60be804271ab0d5fb59eeaefc6e518eb707a67c979c0d5ac6f3e7442ef0de177</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:43:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T12:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-flexes-climate-action-muscle-at-cop31-despite-trump-no-show/a-79968666--20e2652dd010.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-flexes-climate-action-muscle-at-cop31-despite-trump-no-show/a-79968666?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US government is snubbing UN climate talks in Turkey. That's prompted a delegation of American lawmakers, mayors and governors to make the trip instead, aiming to show climate action in the US is alive and well.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Students' List candidates take seats as Serbian parliament opens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9d0da2d96f138cf7cebdf28afe9547c4864b60443de9c64cfbd17b5f2bc3a8a</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:43:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T12:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/students-list-candidates-take-seats-as-serbian-parliament-opens/a-79969166--96de93cfad7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/students-list-candidates-take-seats-as-serbian-parliament-opens/a-79969166?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Serbia's Student List's candidates have taken their oaths in the inaugural parliament session. As the new majority, they have 90 days to form a government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp and Wirtz offer glimpse of bright German future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9de64dc9eeddfb59e5c5a4f383be01666963728f1c38bc44383c3e162d248786</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:43:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184--a5059b3200c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's fall from grace in recent years has seen the team drift away from the fans. But Monday's drubbing of the Netherlands and the impact of Jürgen Klopp, Florian Wirtz and emerging youngsters offers hope.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine updates: Russia-Crimea bridge appears destroyed after strike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af7be75da9e8bd0b67aa05fe07ebca2007b14b64dd8bf03effc517ab73900602</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:43:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-russia-crimea-bridge-appears-destroyed-after-strike/live-79964446--dc105376fd38.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-russia-crimea-bridge-appears-destroyed-after-strike/live-79964446?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Zelenskyy said a strike on the Kerch bridge in Crimea was in response to continued Russian attacks targeting his country's infrastructure. Meanwhile, two bridges were hit in Russian attacks on Kyiv. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Could the Airbus' €3 billion loan row reignite a US-EU trade dispute?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e78437cde591b9f7ae22d3611b15bdfdf9eea67b116b39f0d240f888e7c3e3f1</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:43:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-the-airbus-_3-billion-loan-row-reignite-a-us-eu-trade-dispute/a-79943075--30f362f3b820.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-the-airbus-€3-billion-loan-row-reignite-a-us-eu-trade-dispute/a-79943075?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US says a record €3 billion financing package for Airbus may conflict with a transatlantic aircraft-subsidy truce. EU officials insist the funding complies with market-based rules.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Turkish authorities raid opposition Sozcu news channel, appoint new management</title><id>ur